GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Position_SiteCutoverSequencingStrategy> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Position_SiteCutoverSequencingStrategy> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_SiteCutoverSequencingStrategy> ;
    narr:childCount "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "6554c93c5c55a181b729ea30886d1ffe6558631d" ;
    narr:narration """This position holds the sequencing debate for multi-site cutovers. The mainline is [a firm one-site-at-a-time stance with a clean soak gate](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), restated as [a settled decision to sequence singly](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_16). The counterweight is [the case for pairing two sites that share a dispatch desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12), grounded in a desk-level grievance running since [June](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12). Two rebuttals qualify that pairing case: [the desk pain is a solvable rota problem while a double cutover is not](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15), and [the trade-off framing that a contained pain with a named owner beats an unbounded one](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13). The graph holds the tension open — no reconciliation has landed.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_16> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "We do this one site at a time. A site goes live, it soaks, and only when that soak is clean do we start the next one." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "No parallel cutovers, not even for the two small ones." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The argument for taking Northgate and Ferry Road together is that they share a dispatch desk." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Running two systems at one desk for a few weeks is a known, contained pain with a named owner. Two cutovers landing in the same week is an unbounded one, and we've got nobody to hand it to." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "And the desk supervisor's pain is a rota problem, which is solvable. A double cutover is a staffing problem and a data problem at the same time, which isn't." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The pairing case for the two desk-sharing sites — driven by a supervisor grievance — stands against the dominant one-at-a-time decision and was heard, not adopted." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The rebuttals reframe the desk pain as solvable rota work, but the underlying local-site friction remains unresolved rather than refuted." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13> ] ;
    narr:writer "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:nitro" .
}